# Phase 5 — Jira integration

Only now should Jira enter the architecture.

Start read-only.

Given:

```text
ABC-123
```

DevDesk retrieves:

```text
Summary
Description
Status
Assignee
Acceptance criteria
Recent comments
Jira URL
```

You should be able to do something like:

```text
+ Add Jira Task

ABC-123
```

and have DevDesk populate everything automatically.

Later you can add Jira comments/status changes.

Don't do Jira write operations initially.

---

# Phase 6 — Git integration

This comes **before AI** because AI needs this context.

DevDesk detects your repository and current branch.

For example:

```text
Branch

feature/ABC-123-contract-generation
```

DevDesk recognizes:

```text
ABC-123
```

and associates it automatically.

Now the task can know:

```text
Jira
ABC-123

Repository
customer-salesforce

Branch
feature/ABC-123-contract-generation

Changed files
AccountService.cls
AccountServiceTest.cls
contractGenerator.js
```

Eventually add PR detection.

This dramatically improves the AI context later.

---

# Phase 7 — AI Context Builder + Work Assistant

Don't start by building a chatbot.

Build the **Context Builder** first.

For the current task it assembles:

```text
TASK
ABC-123

CLIENT
Client A

JIRA
description
acceptance criteria
comments

WORK
next action
developer notes
previous activity

GIT
repository
branch
changed files
diff

TIME
sessions
time spent
```

Then AI actions consume this context.

Your first AI button should probably be:

### Resume Task

You return to ABC-123 after several hours.

Click:

**AI → Resume**

DevDesk generates something like:

> You're modifying contract generation for ABC-123.
>
> You identified that `AccountService.getContractAccount()` can return null when the billing account isn't populated.
>
> You modified `AccountService.cls` but haven't updated the corresponding test.
>
> Next action: reproduce the null case and add coverage to `AccountServiceTest.cls`.

That directly solves your context-switching problem.

Then add:

**Summarize Jira**

**Draft Client Update**

**Draft PR Description**

**Summarize Today's Work**

