# Phase 9 — Outlook

I deliberately put Outlook late.

Your current process is:

```text
Jira
 ↓
Outlook email
 ↓
Pin email
 ↓
Remember task
```

Eventually DevDesk replaces that with:

```text
Jira notification
        ↓
     Outlook
        ↓
    DevDesk
        ↓
Task created/updated
```

Example:

```text
New Jira assignment detected

ABC-422
Fix opportunity validation

[Add] [Ignore]
```

A comment notification could simply update the existing task:

```text
ABC-123

New comment from client
```

At that point you should need pinned Jira emails far less.

---

# Phase 10 — Agents and automation

Only after everything above works should you make DevDesk proactive.

Examples:

**Forgotten task**

> ABC-123 has been PAUSED for two days but has an open PR.

**Possible completion**

> PR #142 for ABC-123 was merged. Mark task Done?

**Missing PR**

> ABC-456 has 2h 14m of work and modified files but no associated PR.

**Time anomaly**

> You worked on ABC-123 between 14:02–16:43 but the session is still running.

The AI proposes actions rather than silently changing your work state.

